=== iter-1 progress 10:08Z ===
Tile capture converged over 6 runs. Defects found and fixed, in order:
  1. PNGs never forced to TextureImporterType.Sprite -> Resources.Load<Sprite> null -> every tile
     hidden. This is the one Cesar saw ("all pop ups are lacking images").
  2. Shot area computed as a band between "top chrome" and "bottom chrome"; PowerHUD sits at the
     BALL's height on the right and was classified as bottom chrome, collapsing the band to
     y 100..704 and framing all 12 tiles on empty fairway 600 px above the tee.
  3. FreeSwing driven with ProcessDrag(screenPos) - it takes a LOCAL point, so pull measured 0 and
     steps 1 and 2 were byte-identical. Switched to ExecuteEvents drag, same path a finger takes.
  4. Flick's timing arrow read from a non-existent ShotController.ArrowProgress01 (it lives on
     ShotInputState) -> NaN. Now read off TimingSlabGraphic.CurrentY01, the drawn value.
  5. Subject box = "every graphic under the scheme root" pulled in the 1200x1200 arc and the
     2600x2600 trace. Replaced with explicit per-state subject lists.
  6. Crops still overlapped chrome at any useful size (the 840px analyzer chip cannot clear the
     power gauge). HUD now hidden for the capture; the gate became "no chrome was ACTIVE".
  7. The separation solver kept dodging chrome that was already hidden, cutting the chip in half.
  8. Step-3 tiles taken 0.35s after commit showed the pop alone on grass - the chase camera had
     already swung. Now taken on the FIRST frame the pop/chip appears.

=== iter-1: defects found by the crop sheet and the containment gate ===
9.  HOW IT WORKS bodies did not WRAP. A LayoutElement left at preferredWidth -1 makes the
    HorizontalLayoutGroup ask TMP for the width the SENTENCE wants, not the width left in the row,
    so all three lines ran off the right edge of the panel in play mode - while the edit-mode probe
    measured "990 wide" against the short placeholder key and the fits.* invariants passed, because
    they only asserted the PANEL was on screen. Fixed with preferredWidth 0 + flexibleWidth 1, and
    a new contain.* invariant that measures TMP.textBounds (the GLYPHS) against the panel width.
10. Rebuilding the prefab minted a NEW GUID (DeleteAsset takes the .meta with it), silently
    orphaning the instance in BOTH scenes - no error, the pop-up simply stopped existing. The
    builder now copies to a scratch path and SaveAsPrefabAsset's over the target, which preserves
    the GUID; proven by rebuilding twice and diffing the meta.
11. The re-wire left the orphan behind (it carries a MISSING script, so a
    GetComponentsInChildren<SchemeConfirmModalController> sweep walks past it) - two instances in
    LabScaffold. Cleanup is now by name as well.
12. Saving ShellScene after that baked 2699 lines of anchor churn. Recovered with the documented
    idiom: split the diff into hunks, git apply --cached only the two that are mine (the
    PrefabInstance + the one m_Children line), git checkout the rest. Both scenes are now +107.
13. The node's letter-spacing (-0.78px on EN/Title_2, -1.29px on the footer) was not applied.

